{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760451-werewolf-rites-2e-conversion","id":760451,"title":"Werewolf Rites - 2e Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-07T20:27:46-08:00","id":760451,"title":"Werewolf Rites - 2e Conversion","content":"Has anyone tried to port any of the rites from 1E into 2E, yet? Admittedly, they do provide a basis for fleshing out werewolves in a given locale with regards to ritual magic. That said, I'm posting three of the four seasonal rites from the Rage supplement here, and asking for help on how to tweak them for 2E use, and classify them as either Wolf Rites or Pack Rites. If you guys happen to have any conversions of your own, feel free to post them here. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Bone-Fires of Summer (oooo)</b></u><br /> Summer is the traditional season of war, and the People mark it by building great fires in which they burn war trophies and offerings to their totems. This ritual proclaims their strength and ferocity to the heavens, and empowers their resolution to continue fighting. This rite is typically performed at night, though there is no drawback to performing it under the sun.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The rite begins with the ritemaster appearing, torch in hand, to exhort the gathered werewolves to show their might and resolve to the spirits. As the pyre is lit, the participants throw in war trophies or personal offerings to their pack or tribal totems. Each offering is made with a howl, boast or battle cry. The offerings vary greatly: Hand-carved statuettes, paper money, scalps, delicate origami, leather jackets splashed with the owner's colors are all possibilities. Bones, of course, are the most famous offering, particularly femurs or skulls carved with an account of the former owner and how he died. The ceremony closes with a great howl led by the ritemaster, after which pack alphas usually cry out to their packs to follow them on a hunt. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Summer, ????, ????, ????<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (20 successes; each roll represents 10 minutes' effort)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Success</b></u> All participants in the rite gain five discretionary dice, which may be used toward any action related to combat during the next lunar month. These dice are refreshed each day for the duration of the rite.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Darkest Night of Winter (oooo)</b></u><br /> The most somber of the seasonal rites, the Darkest Night of Winter is a ritual dedicated to endurance and perseverance rather than zeal, strength or wisdom. The rite is always performed when the sky is at its blackest; attempting a spiritual reinforcement of endurance requires adverse conditions. The presence of moonlight at the rite is considered an affirmation of weakness, as if the People were unable to endure poor conditions without the presence of their mother. The participants meet under the open sky, and traditionally wear very little in order to defy the elements. Mountaintops and rooftops are particularly valued gathering places. <br /> <br /> <b>Symbols: </b>Winter, ????, ????, ????<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The ritemaster opens with a ritual greeting and invocation to the spirits, and sets some form of food in the center. The food is traditionally meager for all the werewolves concerned: A single deer carcass for a gathering of multiple packs, or a solitary skinny rabbit for a pack. The rite then moves to an invocation of those who died during the past year. Each participant repeats the names of those Forsaken lost to the packs gathered, and offers some memory, however, short, of the deceased. The ritemaster then divides the food among the werewolves present, stating that even on this meager fare and under this hostile sky, the People will endure. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (20 Successes; each roll represents 10 minutes' effort)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Success</u> </b>All participants in the rite gain five discretionary dice, which may be applied to any action related to enduring physical or mental hardship during the next lunar month. These dice are refreshed each day for the duration of the rite.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit Lamps of Autumn (oooo)</b></u><br /> When the nights begin to grow longer, the power of the Shadow begins to grow as well. Werewolves answer this with the rite called Spirit Lamps of Autumn. This rite offers respect to the spirit world and honors their totems, but also is a demonstration of the Uratha's own strength and vigilance. The lamps lit send a simple message to the spirit world -- We see you. <br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Autumn, ????, ????, ????<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The right begins at twilight, and continues into the deepening night. All werewolves participating in the rite bring spirit lamps they've fashioned themselves to the gathering. These lamps take a great variety of forms. The ritemaster moves from one participant to the next as the rite unfolds, instructing each werewolf to place her lamp at a specific point along a spiral pattern. Each lamp is blessed by the ritemaster in turn, and ritually lit by the werewolf who brought it there. The participant then stands above or beside her lamp (perhaps even holding it), staring out into the growing blackness, and stating her conviction to stand fast against the Shadow. As the ritemaster places and lights the final lamp (always the ritemaster's own), he then speaks out in praise of the totems of the People. The Blood Talons present join in the praise of Destroyer Wolf, the Bone Shadows present join the soft chant to Death Wolf and so on. The ritemaster then names the pack totems of each participating pack, and the packs themselves speak words of thanks and honor. The words vary, but the intent is the same: We see you. We see and honor your strength and wisdom, valued allies. We see and respect your might, enemies, and we will stand against it. We see you. The rite closes as each participant moves beyond the circle of light into the darkness, leaving only the ritemaster in the spiral of light. Many packs move directly into a hunt that very night. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (20 Successes; each roll represents 10 minutes' effort)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Success</b></u> All participants gain five discretionary dice which may be used toward any action related to direct dealings with spirits in the next lunar month. These dice are refreshed each day for the duration of the rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T08:07:01-08:00","id":760667,"title":"","content":"I imagine they all can be made in to Pack Rites, only werewolf specific part should be changed only to Totem ones. Like no need for Tribal invocations in <b>Spirit Lamps of Autumn</b>, only that members are invoking &quot;club motto&quot; ( human tongue sentenced Ban of Totem ). Or that <b>Bone-Fires of Summer</b> could burn offerings and relics from day to day activity of Pack - like bike gang can burn symbols of their rivals and mourn their humans or Wolf-Blooded members. And that howls can be changed to battle cries of gang.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the Seasonal Rites sounds as truly werewolf specific to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:35:16-08:00","id":760793,"title":"","content":"These were translated into a single rite with Harness the Cycle. Nevermind it's a rank 1 rite which you can attempt twice per year. These are rank 4 which you can use once per year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-08-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T15:35:45-08:00","id":760983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760451-werewolf-rites-2e-conversion?p=760667#post760667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine they all can be made in to Pack Rites, only werewolf specific part should be changed only to Totem ones. Like no need for Tribal invocations in <b>Spirit Lamps of Autumn</b>, only that members are invoking &quot;club motto&quot; ( human tongue sentenced Ban of Totem ). Or that <b>Bone-Fires of Summer</b> could burn offerings and relics from day to day activity of Pack - like bike gang can burn symbols of their rivals and mourn their humans or Wolf-Blooded members. And that howls can be changed to battle cries of gang.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the Seasonal Rites sounds as truly werewolf specific to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Noted on that. Will revise accordingly. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These were translated into a single rite with Harness the Cycle. Nevermind it's a rank 1 rite which you can attempt twice per year. These are rank 4 which you can use once per year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will have to check that rite out later. Maybe it'll give me ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Aza